{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-quantum-characteristic-classes-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:quantum-characteristic-classes-unique","kind":"proposition","title":"Uniqueness of quantum characteristic classes","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-quantum-characteristic-classes-exists"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-quantum-characteristic-classes-unique"],"tags":["uniqueness","characteristic-classes","cohomology"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QuantumCharClasses.unique","text":"quantum-characteristic-classes-unique.md","leanSource":"quantum-characteristic-classes-unique.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:quantum-characteristic-classes-unique\"></a><p>Fix a <a href=\"#def:quantum-observable-universe\" data-at=\"quantum-observable-universes/qou-definition\">quantum observable universe</a> and a recursive brane tower <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{A_n\\}_{n \\ge 0}</code>. Each <a href=\"#def:quantum-characteristic-classes\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting-construction\">quantum characteristic class</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa_n \\in H^2(\\mathcal{S}, \\mathcal{B})</code> is uniquely determined as a cohomology class. Two Čech cocycles obtained from different local lifts of the same object of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{G}_n</code> are cohomologous. They represent the same class <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa_n</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-characteristic-classes-unique.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"6.4.6","page":"b/prop-quantum-characteristic-classes-unique","qa":{"counts":{"pass":94,"fai